1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,224
This tutorial follows rent cheques through
Cheque and Cash Collection,

2
00:00:04,224 --> 00:00:08,447
as Maya Khoury, a property manager at
Oasis Crest Properties.

3
00:00:08,447 --> 00:00:12,249
Due lists every cheque whose date has
arrived and

4
00:00:12,249 --> 00:00:15,628
that has not cleared yet, across every
property.

5
00:00:15,628 --> 00:00:20,274
Overdue narrows it to cheques past their
grace period, such as

6
00:00:20,274 --> 00:00:24,497
Fatima Al Zaabi's May cheque, still
waiting to be banked.

7
00:00:24,497 --> 00:00:27,031
To deposit is where banking starts.

8
00:00:27,031 --> 00:00:31,255
Tick the cheques going to the bank today:
Ahmed Hassan's

9
00:00:31,255 --> 00:00:35,479
200104 and Fatima's 300204, both dated the
first of October.

10
00:00:35,479 --> 00:00:39,280
The selected total, 36,750, should match
the deposit slip.

11
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:42,237
Deposit Batch records both as deposited
today,

12
00:00:42,237 --> 00:00:45,193
each into its own property's bank account.

13
00:00:45,193 --> 00:00:48,150
When the bank confirms a cheque has

14
00:00:48,150 --> 00:00:51,106
cleared, find it in the Cheque register.

15
00:00:51,106 --> 00:00:54,063
Ahmed's July cheque, 200103, is still
deposited.

16
00:00:54,063 --> 00:00:58,287
Choose Clear, check the account it cleared
into, and confirm.

17
00:00:58,287 --> 00:01:02,510
It is now Cleared, with its receipt number
beside it.

18
00:01:02,510 --> 00:01:04,200
Not every cheque clears.

19
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:06,311
Fatima's 300204 comes back unpaid.

20
00:01:06,311 --> 00:01:09,268
Choose Bounce, pick the reason the bank

21
00:01:09,268 --> 00:01:11,802
gave, here Payment stopped, and confirm.

22
00:01:11,802 --> 00:01:15,604
Miftah records the return, proposes the
contract's cheque-return charge

23
00:01:15,604 --> 00:01:19,405
of 1,000 for approval, and asks what
happens next.

24
00:01:19,405 --> 00:01:20,672
Choose Replace now.

25
00:01:20,672 --> 00:01:24,896
Fatima hands over a new cheque for the
full 15,500.

26
00:01:24,896 --> 00:01:27,852
Enter its number, 300295, its date, the

27
00:01:27,852 --> 00:01:30,386
fifteenth of October, and its bank.

28
00:01:30,386 --> 00:01:35,032
The replacements cover the whole amount,
so nothing is left owing.

29
00:01:35,032 --> 00:01:35,455
Replace.

30
00:01:35,455 --> 00:01:40,523
The Post-dated view lists the cheques
maturing in the next two weeks

31
00:01:40,523 --> 00:01:45,169
with a running total, and Fatima's new
cheque is already there.

32
00:01:45,169 --> 00:01:48,548
The same story is on each tenancy
contract.

33
00:01:48,548 --> 00:01:53,194
On Ahmed's Cheques tab, 200103 is now
Cleared and 200104 Deposited.

34
00:01:53,194 --> 00:01:56,573
Nothing is ever deleted: every cheque
stays traceable,

35
00:01:56,573 --> 00:01:59,952
from registered to deposited, cleared,
returned or replaced.
